            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Punjabi for rain, then the Punjabi for wind."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ਕੁੱਤਾ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਕੁੱਤਾ — kuttā — \"a dog\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਕੁੱਤਾ (kuttā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from kutta, \"dog\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 3275). CDIAL calls it imitative, comparing Santali kutu kutu, the call to a puppy."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
